From 96ba5ea7f3208a96c595476c2501d75504738f9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 02:10:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] glm: glm_moe_dsa streams take rounds one window at a time;
 TF_GLM_DSA_SHARED=1 shares the decode window (default off)

TensorFold never ran two glm_moe_dsa streams at once: cuda_shared.mixer refused every MLA layer with a rope plane
(error.DsaSharedWindow), so the first concurrent round stopped every rank. Default (this patch): glm_moe_dsa uses the lanes'
"one window a round" mode (Lanes.aloneAtStart; no prompt batching into the shared mixer, Lanes.batchesPrompts), so --parallel > 1
is safe: each round verifies one stream's window through the solo path, exactly as that stream would alone.

TF_GLM_DSA_SHARED=1 (default off): several streams' decode rows share one verify window. cuda_shared.dsaSegs runs the row-wise
projections, router and MoE over every row and each stream's attention per segment (kv rope + latent write, query rope, top-2048
selection and sparse attention on its own caches, offsets dp/q/token lists by the segment's first row; a lone stream passes the
arguments it always did). Solo-only paths (KV split, owner rows, KV shard) stay out of the shared window.

Rank 0 logs the first shared verify (and every 4,096th): "glm lanes: shared verify #N: streams, rows, ms", the stages' evidence that a shared window ran.

Tests: test-glm-dsa-shared-host (the lanes' rule, the startup rule, the prompt batching gate, attend offsets) and
tf-cuda-test glm-conc-rows / glm-conc-rows-e4m3 DIR (one real layer's rows: every stream's decode rows alone and in shared windows
of 2..32 rows give the same bytes; controls: other codebook, swapped picks, same picks with other activations).
Rebased from x7-dsa (K4: passed x7, exact 36/36 + 32/32, aggregate 44.7 tok/s at C=2, 54.8 at C=4 vs 36.7 at C=1) onto 0210.
